    "title": "Knicks vs. Pacers: Start Time, Streaming Live, TV Channel, How to Watch - Bleacher Nation",
    "text": "The Indiana Pacers (15-51) aim to snap a seven-game home losing skid when hosting the New York Knicks (42-25) on Friday, March 13, 2026 at 7:30 p.m. ET. The Knicks are coming off of a 134-117 victory against the Jazz in their most recent outing on Wednesday. The Pacers fell in their last outing 123-108 against the Suns on Thursday. Jalen Brunson’s team-leading 28 points paced the Knicks in the win. Andrew Nembhard recorded 23 points, zero rebounds and two assists for the Pacers. When is Knicks vs. Pacers? This matchup between the Knicks and Pacers is scheduled to tip off on Friday, March 13, 2026. Be ready to see the opening tip at 7:30 p.m. ET. Where to watch Knicks vs. Pacers The Knicks and Pacers will take to the court at Gainbridge Fieldhouse for this matchup on March 13, and if you want to see the action live, get your tickets now from Vivid Seats! What channel is the game on? You can catch this game live on MSG, FDSIN. Knicks vs. Pacers Game Preview Knicks Stats, Odds & Insights This season, the Knicks have been favored 53 times and won 37, or 69.8%, of those games. The Knicks put up 117.2 points per game (only 2.8 fewer points than the 120.0 the Pacers allow). The Knicks make 14.7 three-pointers per game (fifth-most in the league) compared to their opponents’ 13.7. They shoot 37.4% from deep while their opponents hit 35.8% from long range. So far in the 2025-26 campaign, the Knicks score 2.5 more points per home game on average than on the road (118.5 at home, 116.0 on the road), but are conceding 2.6 fewer points per home game compared to road games (109.6 at home, 112.2 on the road). The Knicks have seen a downturn in scoring recently, racking up 114.2 points per game in their last 10 contests, 3.0 points fewer than the 117.2 they’ve scored this season. Pacers Stats, Odds & Insights The Pacers put up 111.3 points per game (27th in league) while allowing 120.0 per outing (25th in NBA). They have a -572 scoring differential and have been outscored by 8.7 points per game. The Pacers score an average of 111.3 points per game. That’s just 0.4 more points than the 110.9 the Knicks allow. With 12.9 made 3-pointers per game and shooting 34.4% from downtown, the Pacers are 18th and 25th in the NBA, respectively, in those categories. At home the Pacers are better offensively, scoring 113.9 points per game, compared to 108.8 on the road. They’re also better defensively, giving up 119.0 points per game at home, and 120.9 away. The Pacers are tallying 112.9 points per game in their previous 10 games, compared to their season average of 111.3. Knicks Key Players to Watch Knicks Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Jalen Brunson 62 26.2 3.5 6.5 0.7 0.1 2.8 Karl-Anthony Towns 63 20.0 11.9 2.9 0.9 0.6 1.6 OG Anunoby 53 16.6 5.2 2.2 1.7 0.7 2.2 Mikal Bridges 67 15.0 4.1 3.9 1.4 0.8 2.0 Josh Hart 54 11.8 7.6 5.1 1.1 0.3 1.4 Pacers Key Players to Watch Pacers Leaders Name GP PTS REB ASST STL BLK 3PM Pascal Siakam 55 24.0 6.7 3.9 1.1 0.4 1.7 Andrew Nembhard 51 17.2 2.8 7.3 0.9 0.1 1.9 Ivica Zubac 44 14.3 10.9 2.2 0.4 0.8 0.0 Aaron Nesmith 37 13.1 4.5 2.1 0.6 0.6 2.2 Jarace Walker 65 11.1 5.0 2.3 0.8 0.3 1.6 Read more NBA Game previews as well as view the latest live NBA lines on Betsperts. Get the latest NBA picks and predictions as well as the daily top NBA Player Prop Bets to choose from. Or, if you are new to sports betting, read our in-depth guide on how to bet on basketball as well as find the best NBA betting sites.",
